 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "OvenFurnaceAdvisor ⊣ Oven & Furnace Plant Operations Governor,
 langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant OPERATIONS
 COORDINATION actor for industrial-scale oven/furnace/furnace-burner
 manufacturing (fabrication/assembly/thermal-test-bench lines producing
 finished industrial ovens, heat-treatment furnaces, melting furnaces
 and furnace burners) -- not direct fabrication/assembly-line-equipment
 control authority and not safety-certification authority (e.g. UL
 795/UL 726 commercial-industrial gas/oil-fired equipment listing, CSA
 certification, or CE marking under the EU Gas Appliances Regulation
 2016/426 for furnace-burner combustion equipment). Four ops
 (`:log-production-batch` / `:schedule-maintenance` /
 `:flag-safety-concern` / `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect
 :propose` only. Twelve concrete governor checks elaborate this
 blueprint's four HARD invariants: propose-only effect, closed op
 allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct fabrication/
 assembly-line-equipment control), permanent equipment-actuate block,
 permanent safety-certification-authority block (this actor never
 self-issues a UL/CSA/CE combustion-equipment safety-certification
 mark), independent equipment verification/registration before
 maintenance scheduling, independent batch verification/registration
 before shipment coordination, independent shipment-quantity recompute
 against the batch's own logged production quantity, double-schedule
 guard, product-type validation, thermal-test plausibility validation,
 and defect-rate plausibility validation. Safety-concern flagging
 (equipment-safety/burner-combustion-safety concern) ALWAYS escalates
 to a human plant supervisor; `:log-production-batch` is the only op
 eligible to auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
